  "design": {
    "decision": "Win tricks that start with a small lead, including partner's low leads and opponents' leads meant to bust a nil.",
    "opponent": "Visible on the first win; opponents stop leading low into the team.",
    "rationale": "It uses the led-card filter, so the reward depends on how tricks are led. That supports protecting a nil and leading low without naming a future payoff.",
